cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "latencynet: end-to-end tail-latency prediction for staged embedded pipelines"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-05
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Predicts the p99 and p99.9 end-to-end latency of a serial staged pipeline
  from a short aligned per-stage probe trace. Three predictors with prediction
  intervals, compared on held-out pipelines in two stage-dependence regimes: an
  analytic sum-of-stages model whose moment identities are exact to machine
  precision and whose Fenton-Wilkinson tail map is measured to under-predict
  p99.9 by 2.4 to 4.3 per cent; an ordinary least squares fit on thirteen probe
  features with the exact Student-t prediction interval; and a gradient-boosted
  tree ensemble with quantile-loss interval heads. Split-conformal calibration
  for all three. Validation level 2. The recorded result is that the learned
  model helps only where stage latencies are dependent, and that the linear
  baseline wins every comparison. Not flight-qualified, not certified, not
  approved for operational aerospace use.
authors:
  - name: "OPTIMA Organisation"
keywords:
  - latency
  - tail-latency
  - percentile
  - prediction-interval
  - conformal-prediction
  - order-statistics
  - embedded
  - real-time
